  "practice": [
    "Say দ three times with the tongue near the teeth: dô, dô, dô.",
    "Practice the vowel forms: দ (dô), দা (da), দি (di), দী (di), দু (du), দূ (du), দে (de), দৈ (doi), দো (do), and দৌ (dou).",
    "Read the combinations aloud: দ + া = দা as in দাম, দ + ি = দি as in দিন, দ + ু = দু as in দুধ, দ + ূ = দূ as in দূর, দ + ে = দে as in দেশ, দ + ৈ = দৈ as in দৈনিক, দ + ো = দো as in দোষ, and দ + ৌ = দৌ as in দৌড়.",
    "Compare দ (d) with ধ (dh, extra air): দাদা / ধান, দাম / ধরা, দিন / ধীরে, and দুধ / ধন্যবাদ.",
    "Use দাও, দেখো, দিন, দুই, দরজা, দরকার, দাম, দুধ, দেশ, দেরি, দোষ, and দৌড় as quick reading anchors.",
    "Recognize these phrases instantly: এটা দাও, এটা দেখো, আমার দরকার, দাম কত, and দরজা খোলো."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "দ is one of the most common Bangla consonants. Its name is dô and its sound is roughly d, pronounced with the tongue closer to the teeth than the English d.",
    "দ and ধ are closely related: দ has a d sound, while ধ has an aspirated dh sound with an extra burst of air.",
    "Compare দাম (dam, price), দিন (din, day), দুধ (dudh, milk), and দরজা (dorja, door) with ধান (dhan, paddy), ধরা (dhora, hold/catch), ধীরে (dhire, slowly), and ধন্যবাদ (dhonnobad, thank you).",
    "Best words to memorize include দাও, দেওয়া, দেখা, দেখো, দেখানো, দিন, দুই, দশ, দরজা, দরকার, দাম, দামি, দিক, দোকান, দুধ, দুপুর, দুঃখিত, দূর, দেশ, দেরি, দোষ, and দৌড়."
